.TH RELAYFSD 1 "2026-11-09" "relayfsd 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
relayfsd \- watch a directory and transfer new files over SFTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B relayfsd
.br
.B relayfsd \-\-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B relayfsd
watches a directory for new files and copies each one to another
machine over SFTP. It runs in the foreground until it is stopped, and is
normally run as a systemd user service.
.PP
It works in one of two directions:
.TP
.B local \(-> remote
A local directory is watched with inotify, including any subdirectories
created later. Each new file is uploaded to
.I remote_dir
on the server. This is the default.
.TP
.B remote \(-> local
A remote directory is polled over SFTP every 10 seconds. Each new file
is downloaded to the local
.IR watch_path .
Files already in the remote directory when
.B relayfsd
first connects are not downloaded.
.PP
If the server cannot be reached,
.B relayfsd
waits and tries again, doubling the delay each time up to 5 minutes. It
logs once when the server goes offline and once when it comes back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config
Run the interactive setup wizard, then exit. The wizard asks for the
server address, login details, the directions to sync in, the directories
to use, what to do with local files after upload, and Discord
notifications. Each prompt shows the current value; press Enter to keep
it. The result is written to
.IR data.json .
.PP
With no options,
.B relayfsd
loads
.I data.json
and starts watching. If the file is missing, it prints a message telling
you to run
.B relayfsd \-\-config
and exits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored as JSON in
.I data.json
in the current working directory, created with mode 0600. The keys are:
.TP
.B ip
Hostname or IP address of the server. The SSH connection always uses
port 22.
.TP
.B username
SSH user name.
.TP
.B auth_method
.B key
or
.BR password .
If unset,
.B password
is used, so configurations written before key support keep working.
.TP
.B key_path
Private key file for
.B key
authentication. A leading
.I \(ti/
is expanded to the home directory. The wizard suggests
.IR \(ti/.ssh/id_ed25519 .
.TP
.B key_passphrase
Passphrase for an encrypted private key. Leave unset if the key has none.
.TP
.B password
SSH password for
.B password
authentication. Choosing
.B key
in the wizard removes this from the file.
.TP
.B watch_side
.B local
(default) or
.BR remote :
which side to watch for new files.
.TP
.B dest_side
.B remote
(default) or
.BR local :
which side to send new files to. It must be the opposite of
.BR watch_side ;
other combinations are logged as unsupported and nothing is copied.
.TP
.B watch_path
The local directory. It is the directory being watched when
.B watch_side
is
.BR local ,
and the download target when it is
.BR remote .
.TP
.B remote_dir
The remote directory. It is the upload target when
.B watch_side
is
.BR local ,
and the directory being polled when it is
.BR remote .
.TP
.B after_upload
What to do with a local file after it has been uploaded:
.B keep
(default) leaves it alone,
.B move
moves it to
.IR move_dir ,
and
.B delete
removes it permanently. This only applies in the local \(-> remote
direction and is ignored otherwise.
.TP
.B move_dir
Destination directory when
.B after_upload
is
.BR move .
It is created if it does not exist. It must not be inside
.IR watch_path ,
or moved files would be uploaded again. If a file with the same name
already exists there, a
.RI \(dq " (1)" \(dq
suffix (or a higher number) is added before the extension.
.TP
.B notifications.discord.enabled
.B true
to post messages to a Discord webhook.
.TP
.B notifications.discord.webhook_url
The Discord webhook URL.
.SS After-upload safeguards
A local file is moved or deleted only when all of these hold:
.IP \(bu 2
the remote copy exists and has the same size as the bytes uploaded;
.IP \(bu 2
the local file's size and modification time did not change during the
upload. A file that is still being written is left in place.
.PP
When
.B after_upload
is
.BR delete ,
the wizard asks you to type
.B yes
before enabling it. Every move, delete, skip and failure is logged, and
failures also send a Discord notification.
.SH FILES
Both files are relative to the current working directory. The supplied
systemd unit sets this to the user's home directory.
.TP
.I data.json
Configuration file. See
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.TP
.I relayfsd.log
Log file, appended to on every run. Lines have the form
.RI \(dq "date time LEVEL | message" \(dq,
where
.I LEVEL
is
.BR INFO ,
.BR WARN ,
.BR ERROR " or " FATAL .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/relayfsd.service
systemd user unit. It runs
.B relayfsd
from the home directory and restarts it 30 seconds after a failure.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
With Discord notifications enabled,
.B relayfsd
posts a message when a file has been transferred, when a transfer fails,
when a move or delete after upload fails, and when an offline server
comes back online.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The wizard finished, or the watcher stopped normally.
.TP
.B 1
The configuration is missing or cannot be parsed, the SSH key cannot be
loaded, the authentication or after-upload settings are invalid, the
configuration could not be saved, or the watcher failed to start.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up a key and configure
.B relayfsd
to use it:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ ssh\-keygen \-t ed25519
$ ssh\-copy\-id user@server
$ relayfsd \-\-config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run in the background as a user service, starting at login:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now relayfsd
.EE
.RE
.PP
Follow the log:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ tail \-f \(ti/relayfsd.log
.EE
.RE
.PP
A minimal
.I data.json
that uploads new files and moves the originals afterwards:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
{
  "ip": "192.168.1.20",
  "username": "user",
  "auth_method": "key",
  "key_path": "\(ti/.ssh/id_ed25519",
  "watch_side": "local",
  "dest_side": "remote",
  "watch_path": "/home/user/outbox",
  "remote_dir": "/srv/inbox",
  "after_upload": "move",
  "move_dir": "/home/user/sent",
  "notifications": {
    "discord": { "enabled": false, "webhook_url": "" }
  }
}
.EE
.RE
.SH SECURITY
The server's host key is not checked, so
.B relayfsd
cannot detect a man-in-the-middle on an untrusted network.
.PP
Passwords and key passphrases are stored in plain text in
.IR data.json .
Key authentication without a passphrase is recommended; it keeps
.I data.json
free of secrets.
.SH BUGS
Files are transferred to a single flat directory. Subdirectory structure
is not kept, and a file with the same name as an existing one overwrites
it.
.PP
In the local \(-> remote direction, a file is uploaded as soon as it is
created. If it is still being written, only part of it may be uploaded.
.PP
In the remote \(-> local direction, only files directly inside
.I remote_dir
are seen; subdirectories are ignored.
.PP
The SSH port is fixed at 22.
.PP
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/Almutairi0/relayfsd/issues
the issue tracker
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR ssh\-copy\-id (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR inotify (7)
